BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-01@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T120000Z
DTEND:20260814T220000Z
SUMMARY:🟢 Convention Registration
LOCATION:11 Dorrance Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Attendees pick up their convention badges at the registration 
 table on the second floor landing of the Graduate Hotel. Print your Event
 brite pass or ticket (or have it ready to scan on a smartphone) to redeem
  for a badge. Requires a convention pass\; registration itself is free to
  process. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/
 necronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-01
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-01
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-02@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T120000Z
DTEND:20260814T133000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Tainted and Impure: Environmental Contamination in the Weird
LOCATION:1 West Exchange Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:A discussion on the feeling of "ick" and our response to real 
 and imagined environmental contamination — how ideas of purity and poll
 ution are entwined\, and what they mean from a moral\, literary\, and sci
 entific perspective. Panelists: Rick Claypool (Moderator)\, Chesya Burke\
 , Eric Schaller\, K. H. Vaughan\, Mathilda Zeller. Full listing: https://
 github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-
 02
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-02
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-03@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T120000Z
DTEND:20260814T133000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Daphne du Maurier: A Strange Creature
LOCATION:1 West Exchange Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Du Maurier (English\, 1907–1989) wrote broadly\, including r
 omantic\, historical\, adventure\, and biography\, often with an underlyi
 ng hint of darkness or the supernatural\, as in Don't Look Now\, The Appl
 e Tree\, The Blue Lenses\, and The Birds. Panelists discuss her work\, co
 ntroversies\, and legacy. Panelists: Adam Golaski (Moderator)\, Victoria 
 Dalpe\, Robert Levy\, Anya Martin. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/
 todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-03
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-03
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-04@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T120000Z
DTEND:20260814T133000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Pre-Lovecraft Sources of Cosmic Horror
LOCATION:11 Dorrance Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Practitioners\, and even masters\, of cosmic horror existed be
 fore Lovecraft\, and were powerful influences on his work. Poe\, Blackwoo
 d\, Bierce\, Machen\, Chambers\, and Dunsany are inevitably cited — but
  to what extent did HPL capture and solidify previous work\, and at what 
 point did his cosmic horror take on a life of its own? Panelists: Matthew
  Carpenter (Moderator)\, Leslie S. Klinger\, Will Murray\, Peter Rawlik. 
 Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomic
 on-2026/README.md#fri-04
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-04
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-05@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T120000Z
DTEND:20260814T133000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 A People's History of The Cthulhu Mythos: Leftist Appraisal a
 nd Reinterpretation
LOCATION:11 Dorrance Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Are colonialism\, capitalism\, and racism inherent in the foun
 dation of the Mythos? What is the textual role of class in Lovecraft's wo
 rk\, and how have recent works attempted to reimagine or critique its und
 erlying ideologies? Panelists: Edward Guimont (Moderator)\, Alexander Dic
 kow\, Khora Martel\, Tonya Monteforte\, Eric Williams. Full listing: http
 s://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/README.md#
 fri-05
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-05
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-06@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T120000Z
DTEND:20260814T133000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Author Readings
LOCATION:11 Dorrance Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Readings by Matthew M Bartlett\, Nathan Carson\, Cody Goodfell
 ow\, and Darrell Schweitzer. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/b
 lob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-06
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-06
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-07@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T133000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
SUMMARY:🟣 Armitage Session 1: Weird Fiction Itineraries — Literary Ge
 ography and Archival Landscapes
LOCATION:1 West Exchange Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Academic paper session chaired by Eric Steinhart. Papers: Dani
 el J. Holmes\, "From Quebec to Kadath: Echoes of Canada in Lovecraft's La
 te Fiction"\; Heather Miller\, "'Vigilant and Insomniac Rationality' in C
 onrad and Lovecraft"\; Katherine Kerestman\, "Galahad in the Rubble: Fran
 k Belknap Long's Letters to Donald Wandrei\, 1927–1975." Full listing: 
 https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/README
 .md#fri-07
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-07
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-08@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T133000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Environmental Activism and Weird Fiction
LOCATION:1 West Exchange Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Climate change\, invasive species\, and habitat destruction ar
 en't foreign concepts in the world of the Weird\, which uses these disast
 ers to fuel its surreal landscapes and uncanny phenomena. Panelists discu
 ss how weird fiction inspires calls to action. Panelists: Rick Claypool (
 Moderator)\, Chesya Burke\, Timothy J. Jarvis\, Victoria Nations\, Jon Pa
 dgett. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/nec
 ronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-08
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-08
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-09@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T133000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Ars Necronomica Panel
LOCATION:1 West Exchange Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Artists from this year's art show at AS220 discuss their work 
 and inspirations\, and what's happening in the world of weird art. Paneli
 sts: Ted DiLucia\, Stephen Gervais\, Kurt Komoda\, Liv Rainey-Smith\, Kay
 te Terry. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/
 necronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-09
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-09
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-10@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T133000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Theosophy and Weird Fiction: How Did the Esoterica of Madame 
 Blavatsky Influence Cosmic Horror
LOCATION:11 Dorrance Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:The esoterica of theosophy may have influenced major weird fic
 tion writers of the 1920s and 1930s\, including Lovecraft\, Machen\, Duns
 any\, Howard\, and Smith. Did the commonalities come from direct influenc
 e\, second-hand\, or a broader cultural zeitgeist? Panelists: Curtis M. L
 awson (Moderator)\, Kenneth Hite\, Sean Moreland\, Eric Williams\, Justin
  Woodman. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/
 necronomicon-2026/README.md#fri-10
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-10
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fri-11@necronomicon-2026.todb
DTSTAMP:20260814T140220Z
DTSTART:20260814T133000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
SUMMARY:🔵 Corporate Horror
LOCATION:11 Dorrance Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:Cubicles\, paperwork\, horrible bosses\, and unseen masters 
 — Ligotti\, Ballard\, and others have explored the strange and terrifyi
 ng world under the baleful eye of corporate ownership. Panelists explore 
 how Late-Stage Capitalism's 9-5 serves as a backdrop for the Cosmic's the
 mes of existentialism and human insignificance. Panelists: John Foster (M
 oderator)\, Gillian Daniels\, Errick Nunnally\, Jeff VanderMeer. Full lis
 ting: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/
 README.md#fri-11
URL:https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecraft/necronomicon-2026/REA
 DME.md#fri-11
END:VEVENT
