SUMMARY:🔵 "Line My Eyes and Call Me Pretty": Sublimation of the Feminin
 e through the Monstrous in Contemporary Horror Literature
LOCATION:1 West Exchange Street\, Providence\, RI
DESCRIPTION:"Monsters are the bedtime stories the patriarchy tells itself.
 " Panelists discuss how the "monster" is used to sublimate or "other" the
  feminine in contemporary horror\, and how effective women authors are at
  reclaiming agency by co-opting monstrosity. Panelists: Anya Martin (Mode
 rator)\, Nadia Bulkin\, Lauren Elise (L. E.) Daniels\, Kristin Dearborn\,
  Jess Lewis. Full listing: https://github.com/todb/todb/blob/main/lovecra
 ft/necronomicon-2026/README.md#sat-02
